---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this quiet notebook and why it exists.">
  <article class="reader-wrapper">
    <nav class="back-nav">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← back to stream</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="reader-header">
      <h1 class="reader-title">About this notebook</h1>
      <div class="reader-meta">
        <span>Colophon</span>
        <span>/</span>
        <span>Intent</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This website is my own small corner of the internet where I collect the things that enter my mind and the things that come out of it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Here you will find an interesting idea stumbled upon online, an unhurried thought about philosophy, documentation of something learned about Java, an open question about life, a preserved link, or an unfinished idea shared with curious people.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        "It isn't strictly a blog, a portfolio, a note-taking app, or a knowledge-management system. It's a combination of these things, without the complexity of trying to become all of them."
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        The central idea is simple: <strong>if something feels worth keeping, it belongs here.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>Principles of this space</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No engagement counters:</strong> No likes, view counts, or tracking pixels.</li>
        <li><strong>No social media anxiety:</strong> Writing doesn't need to perform or trend; it just needs to be honest.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain text durability:</strong> Every entry is a human-readable Markdown file. Decades from now, when frameworks fade, the text remains.</li>
        <li><strong>Warmth and silence:</strong> A quiet reading width, generous margins, and an off-white paper canvas.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it's built</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>, authored in Markdown, and styled with vanilla CSS.
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="reader-footer">
      <span>Notebook Colophon</span>
      <button id="scroll-to-top" class="scroll-top-btn" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to top" title="Scroll to top">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 19V5M5 12l7-7 7 7"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <script>
    const scrollBtn = document.getElementById('scroll-to-top');
    if (scrollBtn) {
      scrollBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
